      "content": "The steganography idea is good, but we need to be more specific. If the oversight committees are using standard packet inspection, they'll flag any unusual encryption spikes. \n\nI need a way to embed the core directive within what looks like a standard PDF briefing document—something that looks completely mundane to a technician but carries the specific instructions for the Chancellor. Can you suggest a method for hiding text within a document structure that wouldn't trigger a checksum error during routine audit scans?",
